 3. 📚 A Thanksgiving gift 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Cover: Authors Equity

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 I joyfully file this newsletter 365 days a year — and Axios feels privileged to be able to bring it to you for free. Here's my Thanksgiving ask: I'd be grateful if you'd take two minutes to preorder my best friend and co-founder Jim VandeHei's new book, " You Control YOU ," for your family, team and friends.

 Why it matters: There's so little for our young people that's encouraging &amp; empowering. Jim has a healthy, actionable "anti-doom manual" to help the next generation win in life and at work. "You Control YOU" reflects Jim's &amp; my shared view of the world, informed by countless generous people who've taught us a better way to live.

 The book is aimed at high school and college students, as well as 20- and 30-somethings, but is useful for all of us. 🎓 Bonus incentive: Jim and I don't keep a dime from our books. Advances and proceeds go to his family's Zotheka Foundation, where every dollar goes to high school grads who can't otherwise afford college. Jim's wife, Autumn, mentors each of them and helps arrange enviable internships.

