 6. 📝 Dario&#x27;s response on free will 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Via X 

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei rejected the notion that humans should surrender free will to AI, offering his  most definitive view  on the question after Axios reported a growing ideological divide among top AI executives.

 Why it matters: These are Amodei's most significant public remarks since the company went public last week, Axios' Madison Mills writes . 🔬 Zoom in: Amodei said that "we should never sacrifice legitimacy or self-determination at the altar of efficiency or security."

 He distinguished between handing over governance to AI, which he opposes, and automating specific tasks, on which he holds more nuanced views. He also said it may make sense to slow or stop certain AI deployments to mitigate job disruption and limit AI's ability to autonomously develop more powerful systems. He took aim at rival AI executives, accusing them of engaging in "vibes-based commercial and political positioning." 🏛️ Mady's original story lit up X yesterday: Top Dems, including ones eyeing 2028, called for new restrictions on AI development. Sens. Mark Kelly (D-Ariz.), Brian Schatz (D-Hawaii), Chris Van Hollen (D-Md.) and Bernie Sanders (I-Vt.) pushed for immediate action. 

