 8. 🏈 1 for the road: NFL holiday drama 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Aaron Rodgers and Pittsburgh Steelers head coach Mike McCarthy chat before Sunday's game against the Eagles. Photo: Michael Owens/Getty Images The Pittsburgh Steelers cut future Hall of Famer Aaron Rodgers yesterday after he torched head coach Mike McCarthy on ESPN's " The Pat McAfee Show ."

 The Steelers benched Rodgers, 42, in favor of backup Mason Rudolph ahead of tomorrow's game against Denver — then released him altogether. Rodgers said he learned about the decision while on the phone with teammates. The four-time NFL MVP painted McCarthy, his longtime coach in Green Bay, as a woefully out-of-touch leader.

 He said McCarthy arrived late to a quarterback meeting, fell asleep twice and walked out "like nothing happened." Rodgers also said McCarthy ended a halftime meeting by saying "1-2-3, Packers!" Go deeper . 

 
 
